SentinelTrade AI: Comprehensive Project Plan

Version: 1.1
Objective: A self-hosted, low-volume long-term investment AI targeting a 4%+ annual return using a Multi-Agent system on private hardware.

1. System Architecture (The "Mental Model")

The system is divided into four distinct logical zones to ensure security and modularity.

A. The Brain (Inference Zone)

Role: Financial analysis, sentiment extraction, and trade thesis generation.

Hardware: Proxmox VM with GPU Passthrough (6x GPUs available).

Model: Llama-3 or Mistral via vLLM / Ollama.

Input: RSS News feeds, SEC filings, Market technicals.

B. The Core (Execution Zone)

Role: Portfolio management, risk calculation, and broker communication.

Logic: Multi-Agent (Analyst -> Risk Manager -> Executor).

Broker: Alpaca Markets (Paper/Live).

Persistence: PostgreSQL for trade logs and audit trails.

C. The Sentinel (Human-in-the-Loop Zone)

Role: Zero-Trust safety layer.

Logic: If trade_value > 2% of portfolio OR daily_turnover > threshold, state = PAUSED.

Notification Stack:

Email: Full trade thesis via SMTP.

SMS: Critical alerts via Twilio.

Dashboard: UI notification with Approve/Deny functionality.

D. The Gateway (Interaction Zone)

Dashboard: React/Tailwind frontend for trade management.

Security: Authelia MFA + Nginx Reverse Proxy (TLS 1.3).

Home Assistant Bridge: Scoped REST API (Read-only) for portfolio monitoring.

2. Infrastructure & Deployment

Hypervisor: Proxmox VE.

Networking: Gigabit/Fiber-ready.

Isolation: The Core VM has no inbound access from the public web; only the Gateway is exposed via proxy.

3. Data Flow & Security Guardrails

Sentiment Check: Brain analyzes news and outputs a Confidence Score (1-10).

Risk Check: Core calculates Position Size based on the score and current Drawdown.

HITL Trigger: If the move is "Risky" or "Large," execution halts.

User Approval: Manual sign-off required via the Secure Dashboard.

Execution: Core sends signed order to Alpaca.

